# Services (Workspace)

**Workspace-specific**: No base rule (project-only patterns)

## Architecture

| Service | Port | Role |
|---------|------|------|
| Stargate | 9999 | Client endpoint, orchestration — sole inference endpoint for both local and cloud models |
| Gateway | container-internal | Inference engine. Runs inside edge container; Edge Stargate reaches it on `localhost:9998` or UDS within the container. Never reachable from host or clients |
| RAG | UDS (default) | Semantic search + knowledge management. ChromaDB vectors, SQLite property index, `articles` table (metadata enriched at query time via `source_hash` join). Article upsert API (`POST /article`) + MCP tool `rag(op="upsert_article", ...)`. Default UDS `/tmp/universal-protocol/rag.sock`, overrideable via `RAG_SOCKET_PATH`; TCP via `rag.host`/`rag.port` in stargate.yaml |
| Cloud Proxy | UDS (default) | OpenRouter relay; default UDS `/tmp/universal-protocol/cloud-proxy.sock`, overrideable via `CLOUD_PROXY_SOCKET_PATH`. Stargate passthrough: `GET /api/models`, `POST /api/select` on :9999 |
| Event Service | UDS | Centralized event store (SQLite). Host subprocess via `./manage`. Ingest: default `/tmp/universal-protocol/events.sock` via `EVENTS_INGEST_SOCK`. Query+Subscribe: default `/tmp/universal-protocol/events-query.sock` via `EVENTS_QUERY_SOCK` (HTTP `POST /v1/query` + WebSocket `GET /v1/subscribe`). Library: `libs/event_store/` |
| MCP Server | 443 (TLS) | Tool server for Cursor + Claude API + xAI Grok agents. Container managed by `./manage` |
| Cortex API | UDS | REST gateway to cortex.db. Host subprocess via `./manage`. Library: `libs/cortex_store/`. Default UDS `/tmp/universal-protocol/cortex-api.sock`, overrideable via `CORTEX_API_SOCK` |
| Agent Bus | UDS | Inter-agent message bus (threads + turns). Host subprocess via `./manage`. Library: `libs/agent_bus_store/`. Default UDS at `/tmp/universal-protocol/agent-bus.sock`, overrideable via `AGENT_BUS_SOCK` |
| Git integration worker | `127.0.0.1:8091` TCP (default) | Git integrate/land/status/diff; host uvicorn subprocess via `./manage`. Stargate forwards `/api/v1/git/*`. Override via `GIT_INTEGRATION_WORKER_HOST` / `GIT_INTEGRATION_WORKER_PORT` |
| Manage controller | UDS | `./manage` TUI + JSON-RPC lifecycle API. Default UDS `/tmp/universal-protocol/manage.sock`, overrideable via `MANAGE_SOCKET`; code SOT: `transport_utils.MANAGE_SOCKET`. Also in `~/.gateway/topology.yaml` → `manage_socket`. Agents: MCP `manage(action="status")` — ¬ probe repo root or `~/.gateway/manage.sock` |

Three roles: **Master** (host, orchestrator), **Relay** (host, forwarding), **Edge** (container, execution).
Default: `Master(host:9999) → Edge(container, Unix socket) + Relay(TCP) → Edge`

Deploy/manage via `./manage` (TUI). Config at `~/.gateway/stargate.yaml`.
See: `topology_ws.mdc`, `systems/federation/TOPOLOGY.md`

### Manage process recycle — tmux `0:0` (seat op)

**Invariant:** `manage.sock` absent ∨ long-lived manage must reload (e.g. edits under
`scripts/model_manager/ui/controller/charter_runner/`) ⇒ **seat** recycles manage
via tmux — ¬ park on the operator (`judgment-escalation-ladder`).

`./manage` on this host usually lives in **tmux session 0 / window 0** (`0:0`).
Confirm with `tmux capture-pane -t 0:0 -p` before sending keys.

| Need | Path |
|---|---|
| Service start/stop/sync_restart (sock up) | MCP `manage(...)` only — Use the `service-lifecycle` skill |
| Manage process itself down / code pickup | tmux `0:0` quit/start recipe below |
| `charter_reload` | Loop bounce only — **not** Python re-import; charter-runner edits still need quit/start |

**Safe quit/start recipe** (fleet stays up across the quit when hold is used):

1. `manage(action="charter_pause", …)` when a tick may be live
2. Poll `manage(action="charter_hold_status")` until `safe_to_quit=true`
3. `tmux send-keys -t 0:0 'q' Enter` (or type `q` in the TUI) — wait for shell prompt
4. `tmux send-keys -t 0:0 'cd /mnt/torus/projects/universal-llm-gateway && ./manage' Enter`
5. Wait until MCP `manage(action="status")` works again (`manage.sock` live)
6. `manage(action="charter_resume")` if a hold was set
7. Re-`start` / `sync_restart` any services that stayed down (e.g. GIW)

**Forbidden:** ask the operator to quit/start manage; `systemctl` / `pkill` / raw
docker kill for lifecycle. **Permitted:** tmux drive of `0:0` for the manage
process; MCP `manage` for everything else once the sock is up.

### Charter control — global vs per-root

| Need | Action | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| Stop **all** admits (fleet) | `charter_pause` / `charter_resume` / `charter_hold_status` | Durable `tick-hold.json` — orthogonal to ledger |
| Hold **one** enrolled root | `charter_block_root(root_id, reason?, clear_wip?)` | Ledger `BLOCKED` + receipt tip + unenroll (default); stops **new** admits only |
| Clear per-root hold | `charter_unblock_root(root_id, reenroll?)` | `BLOCKED` → `IDLE`; re-enroll only when `reenroll=true` |
| Read one root | `charter_root_status(root_id)` | status / enrolled / wip / last_error / operator_hold |

**Invariant:** bus NOTE / WAKE / CHECKPOINT prose alone **never** arms or clears a hold
(6489). Tip `BLOCKED`/`NOTE` posted by `charter_block_root` is a **receipt**, not the
source of truth. In-flight `cursor-sdk` on a blocked root keeps running — cancel still
needs operator auth (`session-abort-authorization`). Spec:
`cortex://notes/system/specs/charter-runner-root-control.md`.

